{"title":"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/5/5753734e29398cf1e59cb67a78e86180c7499f2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d,e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> are real numbers such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/60098488436ab00bf6961ec715b867f633984c7c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a+b+c+d+e=8\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"14\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbc4a1f0afb842215438db2a6b30db9dcfcf50f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2+b^2+c^2+d^2+e^2=16\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Determine the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Cauchy Schwarz, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aa10c86cc9994b95ffa9e48c307dcc8779432c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+1+1+1)(a^2+b^2+c^2+d^2)\\geq (a+b+c+d)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"408\" height=\"19\" />\nthus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba19fad9a55a877e138dae330966544ece3d844f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(16-e^2)\\geq (8-e)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"19\" /> \nFinally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/3/ab3b4b382b1fd74f122b1e45b44b39dad0b49073.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e(5e-16) \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" /> which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/b/90bcf5de2323da81518358445792f6bca7e3ca1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{5} \\geq e \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />\nso the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2cfd6fecc678c13886c4900727231c9743e3b4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><b>from:</b> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://image.ohozaa.com/view2/vUGiXdRQdAPyw036\">Image from Gon Mathcenter.net</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Seeing as we have an inequality with constraints, we can use Lagrange multipliers to solve this problem.\nWe get the following equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eedaad6b14c784ad863133c9ba5da5af1fa0ad7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)\\hspace*{0.5cm} a+b+c+d+e=8\\\\ (2)\\hspace*{0.5cm} a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2}+d^{2}+e^{2}=16\\\\ (3)\\hspace*{0.5cm} 0=\\lambda+2a\\mu\\\\ (4)\\hspace*{0.5cm} 0=\\lambda+2b\\mu\\\\ (5)\\hspace*{0.5cm} 0=\\lambda+2c\\mu\\\\ (6)\\hspace*{0.5cm} 0=\\lambda+2d\\mu\\\\ (7)\\hspace*{0.5cm} 1=\\lambda+2e\\mu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"258\" height=\"137\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb9784238a0e8caf96b491ddba1749e92a41490.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab8ccbedc8ad9dd3e5fb8e654b94ee38f70f19e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> according to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd8597460a07f59450a07e0f94607fcb479cf974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c932ecfb55276fff7c312aa00a4b564c3ec42fc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> according to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/c/d6cd3a9ea70172e12e3fbc63f037b9aa47d4539e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e68935d2f37dda4e0ac9ecb1aaca45556320e0cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />. Setting the right sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/104992efa4deaa9a2dfeeec9b331ad0bf628f80a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" /> equal yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/e/3fe6114068d34ba0c7460dde92e2dd9bd893df55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda+2a \\mu= \\lambda+2b \\mu \\implies 2a\\mu=2b \\mu \\implies a=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"370\" height=\"16\" />. Similar steps yield that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/599d9cb517c93cbd8dbd1ba4e11150975bc490b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b=c=d$\" width=\"107\" height=\"12\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/3/2b38e4181278b1a223bee4781b9b4ca5c9ad4e3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4d+e=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/4275a9fbaea81cc50b99f31b36344da9d9d05de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4d^{2}+e^{2}=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />. Solving the system yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e7015d9b09289c7e4eb458be3b2becdd4196d48f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e=0,\\frac{16}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />, so the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2cfd6fecc678c13886c4900727231c9743e3b4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A re-writing of Solution 1 to avoid the use of Cauchy Schwarz. We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3c9165e35a2d7a37538face90d15d91c5cdaab5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a+b+c+d)^2=(8-e)^2,\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"19\" /> and \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/0/96066232aa4453681790836973926c3d4adecbec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2+b^2+c^2+d^2=16-e^2.\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"16\" />\nThe second equation times 4, then minus the first equation, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/4954ca00a5a394d185cc62632e9245e453582824.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a-b)^2+(a-c)^2+(a-d)^2+(b-c)^2+(b-d)^2+(c-d)^2=4(16-e^2)-(8-e)^2.\\]\" width=\"554\" height=\"19\" />\nThe rest follows.\n</p><p>J.Z.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Principle_of_Insufficient_Reasons\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Principle of Insufficient Reasons\">Principle of Insufficient Reasons</a>, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb60e0857a2c0a2c47acfbe81781032feb1f7150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> are indistinguishable variables, the maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is acheived when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/599d9cb517c93cbd8dbd1ba4e11150975bc490b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b=c=d$\" width=\"107\" height=\"12\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3de8eadf0d5746eccff6d955a3d25db2a5a8f398.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4a+\\max e=8\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c6cba84805b6fe81e81990b594c130d00e53611.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4a^2+(\\max e)^2=16\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/3/5e326122abd9fc057437bdd00f06dd111f2c546f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\max e=\\boxed{\\frac{16}{5}}\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"48\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> ~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001\" title=\"Ddk001\">Ddk001</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Note: For some reason I think this solution is missing something.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO\" title=\"1978 USAMO\">1978 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1978\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016184401\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 240/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7062/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.227      1 -total\n 57.13%    6.985      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 40.92%    5.003      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11372:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016184401 and revision id 238192. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}